{"skill":{"slug":"security-auditor","displayName":"Security Auditor"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770008217892,"changelog":"Initial release – comprehensive security audit and secure coding skill.\n\n- Provides actionable code review for security vulnerabilities and OWASP Top 10 risks.\n- Includes checklists and code patterns for authentication, CORS/CSP headers, input validation, XSS, SQL injection, secrets handling, and more.\n- Offers recommended secure code snippets and sample security headers.\n- Details best practices for dependency scanning, output formatting, and secure architecture review.\n- Supports structured output for clear, actionable security audit results.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":11050,"sha256":"808e854691696a83af77e1c0ab158e84ccde63fd48b4c8a8966068d14629dcae","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2085,"sha256":"ffd66d3bf4ada02e8619a76d99cac1e474ca8c8b60fd60c5990eda404b4f4033","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789027865292,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"0bd0655c4fd874f6f8b59aacc589d794530638a8f06e5cebcdc4565e711cd31b","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/0bd0655c4fd874f6f8b59aacc589d794530638a8f06e5cebcdc4565e711cd31b","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: security-auditor\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is designed to equip an AI agent with the knowledge and processes to perform security audits. The `SKILL.md` file provides extensive guidance on secure coding practices, OWASP Top 10 vulnerabilities, security headers, input validation, authentication best practices, and dependency security. All code examples clearly differentiate between insecure and secure patterns, serving an educational purpose. There is no evidence of malicious intent, data exfiltration, unauthorized execution, persistence, or prompt injection aimed at subverting the agent's intended function; instead, it explicitly promotes secure development and auditing practices.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160816207},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":74,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789027865292},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This security-auditing skill is mostly purpose-aligned, but it mixes review-only metadata with instructions to make sensitive security and dependency changes, including unpinned npm tool execution.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Reviewing authentication, secrets, security headers, and protected files is proportionate for a security auditor, but users should keep that access explicitly task-scoped because these areas are sensitive.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact is a single Markdown skill with no bundled executable scripts or install-time hooks, but it recommends runtime commands such as unpinned npx package execution and dependency update commands.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Triggers are broad and could activate for many general security terms, while the body includes modification-oriented instructions and examples touching auth, secrets, middleware, database schema, and dependency files without explicit approval boundaries.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No persistence, background services, tool hijacking, credential exfiltration, privilege escalation, or hidden cross-session behavior was found in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is security review and OWASP guidance, which fits most content, but the skill also directs design and implementation of authentication, validation, encryption, tests, and dependency fixes despite declaring scope: review.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want a security-review assistant that may advise changes in sensitive parts of a project. Treat its dependency commands as suggestions, not automatic steps: pin or use locally locked tools, review any package changes, and require explicit approval before modifying auth, secrets, middleware, database schema, or package files.","findings":"[OH1] expected: The flagged dangerouslySetInnerHTML snippets are instructional XSS examples showing bad, sanitized, and preferred rendering patterns; they are not skill runtime output handling.\n[PE3] expected: The flagged access-token language appears in a JWT best-practices example using short-lived tokens and environment-provided secrets, not credential-file access or credential theft behavior.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The broad trigger list is real and under-scoped for a high-trust security skill, increasing accidental activation risk.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: The review-scope declaration conflicts with implementation-oriented audit steps and dependency-changing guidance, creating a material scope concern.\n[RP1] unexpected: The skill recommends unpinned npx execution for better-npm-audit and npm-check-updates, and one suggested command mutates dependency declarations.\n[T08] unexpected: The static scan's unpinned third-party package execution concern is supported by the dependency-security command block.\n[T09] expected: The rate-limit example's raw x-forwarded-for usage is a weak code pattern if copied directly, but it is an application-security example rather than hidden skill behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789027865292}}}}}